{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>If a man gives to his neighbor silver or vessels.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded that there are four types of bailees: the unpaid bailee (shomer ḥinnam), the paid bailee (shomer sakhar), the borrower (sho'el), and the renter (sokher), and their laws differ. And this pericah speaks of the unpaid bailee, for it is the way of every person to guard a deposit of silver or of vessels without payment; the pericah after it, ״כי יתן איש אל רעהו חמור או שור או שה וכל בהמה לשמור״, speaks of the paid bailee, for it is not the way to guard animals of others except for payment; and ״וכי ישאל איש מעם רעהו״ — this is the borrower; ״אם שכיר הוא בא בשכרו״ — this is the renter." "<b>And know</b> that the principle of these four bailees is: the unpaid bailee is exempt for everything in cases of theft and loss, and all the more so in cases of accident, and he performs kindness with the owner when he wishes to guard his deposit without payment. The borrower is liable for everything in cases of theft and loss, and even in cases of accident, and he receives kindness from the owner — as our Rabbis of blessed memory said, that all the benefit is his; therefore, with the unpaid bailee, all damages that come upon the property belong to the owner and not to the bailee, and with the borrower, all damages that come upon the property belong to the borrower and not to the owner. The paid bailee and the renter are partners in benefit: this one rents out his animal or his vessels to his fellow and takes his rental fee, and that one uses them; and since the benefit is between them, it is fitting that they divide the damages between them. Damages of theft and loss belong to the paid bailee and to the renter, and not to the owner; and damages of accident — such as ״מת או נשבר או נשבה״ — belong to the owner and not to the paid bailee and the renter. All these are laws of equity and equal measures, statutes and righteous judgments."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:56.883168757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}